{
    "background_story": "Jemma was a brilliant entomologist with a passion for beetles. Her fascination with the Epilachna genus, commonly known as the lady beetles, led her to dedicate her career to studying these tiny creatures. Jemma's groundbreaking research on the Epilachna's unique defense mechanisms and social behaviors earned her international recognition. She spent countless hours in the field, observing and collecting specimens, and was particularly fond of the Epilachna varivestis, with its striking color patterns. Jemma's work not only advanced the scientific understanding of these insects but also helped develop more effective methods for controlling pests and preserving biodiversity. Her dedication to the Epilachna genus inspired a new generation of entomologists and earned her the nickname 'The Lady Beetle Lady'.",
